        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bonny Hills, New South Wales; Port Macquarie; Queensland; Victoria; South Australia; Tasmania; Australia\n- People: Shelley Watts\n- Roles: amateur boxer\n- Organizations: Port Macquarie-Hastings\n- Species: Cyneoterpna wilsoni\n\nFacts:\n- Bonny Hills is a town in New South Wales, Australia, about 30 minutes' drive south of Port Macquarie.\n- As of the 2011 census, Bonny Hills had a population of 2,870 people.\n- Shelley Watts was born on 10 August 1987 in Port Macquarie.\n- Port Macquarie is a coastal town in the local government area of Port Macquarie-Hastings.\n- In June 2016, Port Macquarie and its suburbs had a population of 45,698.\n- Shelley Watts is an Australian amateur boxer.\n- Cyneoterpna wilsoni is found in Queensland, New South Wales, Victoria, South Australia, and Tasmania.",
